package kgen

// opsExtMechanics is the core OPS.md family for ext sub-ops for keyword mechanics, copies and damage. opsEntries (opsdoc.go)
// places it in the document; a new item goes in its own opsdoc_<mechanic>.go.
var opsExtMechanics = []opsDoc{
	{"ex:Adamant", "ExAdamant (N)", "Sub[0] when at least n mana of one colour was spent to cast the source, else Sub[1] (CastSA>Count$Adamant_<n>.<Colour>.<yes>.<no>; gorge effects/count_body_heads.go evalAdamantBranch). N packs the colour index (bits 0-2, W U B R G) and n (bits 3-4, 0-3: the per-colour spend counts saturate at 3). Lowered at three sites, each reading the stack-entry spend (any other site refuses): a spell's own chain reads the resolving entry (Cauldron's Gift, Foreboding Fruit); a self ETB replacement's CheckSVar$ (K:etbCounter Adamant$, the Throne of Eldraine Paladins) reads the spell entering, 0 for a permanent entering any other way; in a self-ETB trigger's CheckSVar$, as the trigger is queued the spell's count is read from the resolving entry (stackEntry.spc) and bound into the pending trigger's x; the resolution recheck reads gorge's: the bound cast-time value while the source is off the battlefield (the departure snapshot, CR 113.7a/608.2h) or the same object on it, 0 for a new object (leaving wiped the live spend, CR 400.7). kop.AdamantLiveRead (bit 5) marks a self-ETB trigger body's ConditionManaSpent$/ConditionManaNotSpent$ gate (gorge effects conditionManaSpentMet), read live: 0 once the source is off the battlefield. Catharsis, Deceit, Emptiness, Vibrance, Wistfulness."},
	{"ex:NotOwnLibMV", "ExNotOwnLibMV", "Inside a RepeatEach over players: the mana values summed of the library cards in the resolution's remembered set that the repeated player does not own, a face-down one skipped (gorge Count$ValidLibrary Card.IsRemembered+!RememberedPlayerOwn$CardManaCost). Parker Luck."},
	{"ex:RemEachOwnNonLand", "ExRemEachOwnNonLand", "Inside a RepeatEach over players: the cards in the resolution's remembered set that are nonland and owned by the repeated player (gorge Remembered$Valid Card.nonLand+RememberedPlayerOwn, the RepeatEach body's ConditionCheckSVar$ gate; the repeated player itself is bound in eachPl, never remembered). Kroxa, Titan of Death's Hunger."},
	{"ex:OppExtreme", "ExOppExtreme (N figure, F)", "A figure over the controller's living opponents in seat order: N's low byte OppExtAmount counts them, OppExtLife / OppExtHand / OppExtGrave / OppExtValid take the highest (OppExtLowest in N: the lowest) life total, hand size, graveyard card count, or count of battlefield permanents matching F read from that opponent's side. OppExtNonTrigPl in N walks every living player but the trigger entry's trigger player instead, the controller included (gorge nonTriggeredTargetGroup: `PlayerCountDefinedNonTriggeredTarget$HighestCardsInHand`, `$HighestLifeTotal`, `$HighestValid <spec>`; Battle Angels of Tyr). OppExtCountCmp in N counts the members whose hand (OppExtHand), graveyard length, a token waiting there included (OppExtGraveAll), spells cast this turn (OppExtSpellsCast, the per-caster turn tally), or the expression Sub[1] read from that member's own side (OppExtMemberExpr: the member's seat is the controller, so a YouCtrl clause names it; Whiplash Trap's `PlayerCountOpponents$ConditionGE2 ThisTurnEntered_Battlefield_Creature.YouCtrl`) compares Op against Sub[0], read once from the controller's side; OppExtAllPl adds the controller to the group (gorge hasPropertyStateBacked: `PlayerCountOpponents$HasPropertyHasCardsInHand_Card_GTY`, `PlayerCountPlayers$HasPropertyHasCardsInGraveyard_Card_GE7`, `PlayerCountOpponents$ConditionGE<n> SpellsCastThisTurn`; Wojek Investigator, Master's Councillors, Mindbreak Trap). OppExtLifeLost takes the highest (OppExtLowest: the lowest) life that member lost this turn (gorge playerCountExtreme's LifeLostThisTurn arm: `PlayerCountRegisteredOpponents$Highest|LowestLifeLostThisTurn`, the living opponents; `PlayerCountDefinedRegistered$...`, every living player with OppExtAllPl, `PlayerCountDefinedRegistered.Other$...`, the opponents; Sygg, Bloodchief Ascension, Knight of the Ebon Legion, Y'shtola). An empty group reads 0. Gorge: `PlayerCountOpponents$Amount`, `$Highest|LowestLifeTotal`, `$Highest|LowestCardsInHand`, `$HighestCardsInGraveyard`, `$Highest|LowestValid <spec>` (opponentGroup, playerGroupCount, lifeExtreme, playerCountExtreme). Bloodghast, Joined Researchers, Claim Jumper, Vault of Champions."},
	{"ex:StepIn", "ExStepIn (N step bits)", "1 while the game's current step is one of the kop.Step bits in N, else 0 (gorge ConditionPhases$ <list>, conditions.go: the ONE phase-name parser engine/state.ParsePhases maps the named gorge steps onto the kernel's numbering; a gorge combat-damage step sets the kernel's first-strike and regular damage bits because gorge models one combat-damage step). kgen also lowers it beside ConditionPlayerTurn$ (the conjunction of a turn test and this step test), with no third Condition*$ key. Great Train Heist."},
	{"ex:PhaseCount", "ExPhaseCount (N)", "The turn's phase ledger (gorge CombatsThisTurn, EndStepsThisTurn, counted as each BeginCombat / End step is entered): N 0 the combats begun, N 1 the finished end steps (Count$FinishedEndOfTurnsThisTurn: begun, less the one being run while in the end step). FirstCombat$ True is N 0 == 1."},
	{"trig:FirstAttack", "Tf3FirstAttack", "An Attacks trigger that fires only for an attacker not yet declared this turn (gorge FirstAttack$ True, trigmatch firstAttackOK: AttacksThisTurn == 1 at the fire): the attackers-declared mark (mechAttackedObj) is read before the declaration sets it. Aurelia the Warleader, Fear of Missing Out."},
	{"ext:PlotGrant", "OpExt ExtPlotGrant (Obj Remembered)", "Every object in the resolution's remembered set that is in exile becomes plotted (CR 702.170b-d; gorge effAlterAttribute Attributes$ Plotted, zone gate ZExile, the fold stamping PlottedTurn): a DurPlot genState.may record stamped with the current turn (StallMayPlay past maxMay), so offerPlotCasts offers its free sorcery-speed cast from exile on a later turn whether or not the card has plot, then the card's own BecomesPlotted triggers. Any other zone is a no-op. Kellan Joins Up."},
	{"ext:Hideaway", "OpExt ExtHideaway (B, C)", "C 0 (Hideaway N, CR 702.75a): the controller looks at the top B cards of their library (all of it when shorter), is asked which to exile face down (ChHideaway, gorge's KChoose hideaway_pick, library order) and puts the rest on the bottom in a random order (backward Fisher-Yates, Rand(i+1); none for one card); the exiled card is linked to the source's incarnation (genState.links with the linkHide bit; a full table first drops the links of departed sources, StallLinks). C 1 (Defined$ ExiledWith, Optional$, WithoutManaCost$): the linked card is offered as a free cast (ChGenCastFree); a land is played at once if its controller is the active player with a land play left (gorge effPlay, beginPlay). gorge keys the link on the object id alone, so a source that left and returned still sees the card; the kernel follows CR 400.7. Collector's Cage."},
	{"ext:CounterLose", "OpExt ExtCounterLose (Obj, C)", "Counter the stack ability in target slot Obj; if its source is still the same artifact, creature or planeswalker on the battlefield it loses all abilities (host-bound LoseAbilities override C) for as long as the resolving source stays on the battlefield (gorge Counter RememberCountered$ + Effect RemoveAllAbilities$ AsLongAsInPlay). Tishana's Tidebinder."},
	{"ext:DrainMana", "OpExt ExtDrainMana (Obj player)", "The player Obj loses all unspent mana (gorge effDrainMana, one events.ManaClear for that seat): the ordinary pool, its restricted batches, the artifact/treasure provenance and the persistent tallies all empty (Forge's clearPool(false), not the step boundary's keep-persistent empty). No decision. Power Sink's unless-payment decline, Mana Short. Defined$ Player (every player) stays refused by kgen: the kernel resolves a single player. DrainMana$ True (the activator adds the drained mana) and RememberDrainedMana$ stay refused by kgen."},
	{"ext:TwoPilesSac", "OpExt ExtTwoPilesSac (Obj, F)", "The resolving controller separates the battlefield permanents matching F that the player Obj controls into two piles (ChGenPileSplit: a permanent per pick, AkDone-closed, picking them all ends it; a one-permanent pool poses no split), that player picks one (ChGenPileChoose: 0 the picks, 1 the rest) and sacrifices it (fireSacAll, leaveAll; gorge effTwoPiles battlefield arm + SacrificeAll IsRemembered, cr-twopiles-battlefield-validcards). Pile A rides genState.sacM. Liliana of the Veil."},
	{"ext:Endure", "OpExt ExtEndure (Obj, B, C)", "The object Obj endures N, N the PA of override C read once (N <= 0 does nothing, CR 701.63b): on the battlefield its controller chooses (ChGenEndure: 0 N +1/+1 counters through the AddCounter replacements, 1 a w_x_x_spirit token B for them set to N/N by override C, permanently); gone, the resolving controller gets the Spirit with no ask. More than one mint (a token doubler) stalls StallEndureN (gorge effEndure, CR 701.63a). The TDM Endure carriers."},
	{"ext:Extort", "OpExt ExtExtort (no operands)", "An Extort trigger's body (CR 702.101a): the resolving controller is asked to pay {W/B} (ChGenPayMode, mode 1 = pay / 0 = decline, matching gorge effExtort's two KModes options; both are always offered, as gorge offers them). On a paid answer one mana of either colour is taken from the payer's pool (ordinary W then B before their persistent units, exactly gorge pay.PayExtortPip; no pip is a paid answer that drains nothing) and each opponent still in the game loses 1 life while the controller gains that many, in AliveFrom(controller) order after the controller (gorge extortDrain's LifeChange events). No targets. The trigger is the printed K:Extort expansion's SpellCast line, or the latent trigger a layer-6 AddKeyword$ Extort grant carries (dirac/act_extort.go). Blind Obedience, Crypt Ghast, Life Insurance, Pontiff of Blight, Tithe Drinker, Treasury Thrull."},
	{"ext:Exploit", "OpExt ExtExploit (no operands)", "The marker half of the K:Exploit enters trigger (CR 702.110a; gorge effExploit): lowered only right after the trigger's optional remembering OpSacrifice of one creature by its controller, so the resolution's remembered set (empty at its start) is exactly what the sacrifice took; each object in it fires the source's TrigExploited lines (dirac/kw_exploit.go). A declined sacrifice fires nothing. The keyword itself has no CardDef bit: kgen admits K:Exploit only beside gorge kwExploit's expansion trigger."},
	{"ext:DistCounters", "OpExt ExtDistCounters (B total, F pool)", "Distribute B +1/+1 counters (the dying source's last-known counters) among creatures the resolving controller picks, no targets (gorge putCounterPickDistribute; Vastwood Hydra): one pick at a time from the pool matching F (seat 0 first, entry order), at least one and at most min(B, pool size), Done after the first; the counters then go round-robin in pick order, the earlier picks taking the remainder. A pool of one takes all B unasked, an empty pool or B of 0 asks nothing; a window past 24 stalls StallLook. dirac/ctr_distpick.go."},
	{"ext:DividedCounters", "OpExt ExtDividedCounters (C target slot N)", "Put the triggering source's last-known +1/+1 counters (X, the trigger entry's LKI) on the objects of target slot N as the controller divided them while putting the trigger on the stack: the slot (TargetSpec.Divide = DivLKIP1P1) takes 0..X targets, each at least 1, the division asked after the targets when there are two or more (more than eight stalls StallXTgt); one target takes all X unasked; a target illegal at resolution loses its share (gorge cr-dies-trigger-divided-counters-lki; CR 601.2d, 603.10a). Quirion Beastcaller. Constant-total form: the slot has Divide = N (a literal 2..8) and 1..N targets; the total is N, divided the same way, one target takes all N (Biogenic Upgrade, Glint Weaver); B.N is its CounterType$ kind (0, +1/+1, by default; Contagion's -2/-1, Splendid Agony's -1/-1). Any-number forms: TargetMin$ 0 makes the literal-N slot 0..N (no target is castable and resolves putting nothing; Picnic Ruiner's Stolen Goodies), and a spell's paid {X} (CounterNum$, TargetMax$ and DividedAsYouChoose$ all one SVar Count$xPaid, P1P1) lowers a TgfBoundsV 0..X slot with Divide = kop.DivMaxV (254): the total is the slot's evaluated maximum, more than eight stalls StallXTgt (Elusive Otter's Grove's Bounty; the literal carriers are Storm the Seedcore, Verdurous Gearhulk, Jugan, the Rising Star and Myojin of Towering Might). Only a root target declaration is lifted: the ability chain's head at depth 1, or the chosen mode's head (Abzan Charm), because gorge divides at announcement and a `SubAbility$` body divides at resolution, so Rhino, Terrible Trampler's enters trigger stays refused."},
	{"ext:ManaChoice", "OpExt ExtManaChoice (B amount, C colour mask | 0x100 for Any, F restriction)", "A loyalty ability's resolving Mana effect over a colour choice (CR 605.1a; gorge effects.askManaChoice): Produced$ Combo <colours> with a constant Amount$ N asks the controller one colour per mana (ChGenManaChoice, mode = W U B R G = 0..4; gorge poses one multi-select of N over the colours repeated per unit), Produced$ Any asks one colour for all N (C bit 8). Each pick adds its mana to the pool at once. `F != 0` (a resolving DB$ Mana's RestrictValid$ Spell.<spec> over Produced$ Combo, CR 106.6; gorge effMana) adds each pick as restricted mana through `addManaRestr` (State.rb; `genPrep.restrF` registers F, `anyMultiR` lets the colours differ; StallRestrSrc past the batches the pool holds); Produced$ Any with F stays refused by kgen. Chandra, Hope's Beacon; Desolation of Smaug."},
	{"ext:LibSweep", "OpExt ExtLibSweep (F)", "Every battlefield permanent matching F (as the resolving controller; Teferi uses ...TargetedPlayerCtrl) leaves for its owner's library: seat 0's battlefield, then seat 1's, one departure batch; each owner's cards that reached the library sit on top in move order (gorge libraryOrderPlacement), then each owner that received a card, a token included, in order of first placement, shuffles its library (gorge effChangeZoneAll Shuffle$ True, changeZoneAllShuffleLibraries); nothing moved, nothing shuffles. Teferi, Temporal Pilgrim."},
	{"ext:TokenPT", "OpExt ExtTokenPT (C)", "Right BEFORE an Ex-form CreateToken: reads override C's P/T (its PA/TA) first, runs that CreateToken in place, then sets each token it minted to those values as a permanent layer-7b set stamped at the mint (gorge effects/token.go TokenPower$/TokenToughness$, CR 111.4, 613.4b). No mint does nothing; each token of an X mint takes the set; a count that is not the op's amount (a token doubler) stalls StallTokenPT. Unwilling Vessel, The Skullspore Nexus, Tumbleweed Rising, Dance of the Tumbleweeds, Abzan Monument."},
	{"ext:CopyNamed", "OpExt ExtCopyNamed (B.N named card's CardID, C CopyFlags byte | exception override+1 << 8)", "CopyPermanent DefinedName$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go: the source is a card of the compiled card universe named by the ability, not an object): the resolving controller creates one token that is a copy of that card (its printed face, CR 707.2), through the CreateToken replacements and entry as an object's copy is. B.N is the table token the named card rides as (kgen's copy-by-name key; the matchup remaps it to its CardID), C packs the CopyFlags byte (TokenTapped$ is CpTapped; the AtEOT$ and RememberTokens$ riders are the same flags; no PumpKeywords$) with the copy exceptions' override index+1 (at most 255) in the byte above, read as OpCopyAsTokenEx reads them. The source names no object, so the copy has no template (no face-down copy, no copy of a copy). No copy count, target, Choices$ or counters (kgen refuses them beside DefinedName$); a name gorge's universe does not hold makes gorge copy nothing, so kgen emits no instruction for it. An Aura, an as-enters choice or a clone election stalls rather than ask. A matchup holding a card-name chooser beside the copier is refused (the chooser narrows gorge's name universe). Mutable Explorer's tapped Mutavault."},
	{"ext:CopyPicked", "OpExt ExtCopyPicked (Obj the picked card, B.N CopyFlags | CopyAttacking, C copy exceptions)", "CopyPermanent Choices$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go, the supportsChoice arm): the resolving controller creates one token copy of the object the preceding OpChooseCard picked (RefChosen), read as OpCopyAsTokenEx reads Obj, B.N and C. kgen lowers the mandatory one-pick over the battlefield filter as that OpChooseCard (one KChoose posed even for a single candidate, none for no candidate) and refuses a copy exception, copy count, pump, remember, target, Defined$ or counters beside it. CopyAttacking (B.N bit 14, TokenAttacking$ True in the controller's own attack trigger): the token enters attacking the opponent (gorge copyAttackRider: players only, so no planeswalker or battle defender and no ask); CpTapped enters it tapped. Nothing picked makes no copy, but the AtEOT$ rider's delayed trigger is still registered (CpSacAtEndDly, CpExileAtEnd; gorge scheduleAtEOTNone, CR 603.7) and does nothing at the end step. An Aura poses its host ask when two or more hosts are legal, and an as-enters choice or a clone election is asked, parking the resolution as any token copy does (a copy of a copy of a clone card still stalls StallCopyAllAsk). Calamity, Galloping Inferno."},
	{"ext:CopyTokenCtr", "OpExt ExtCopyTokenCtr (Obj source, B amount, C counter kind)", "CopyPermanent WithCountersType$ / WithCountersAmount$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go, entryWithCounters): the token copy of Obj enters with B counters of kind C, put through the counter replacements as part of the token's own entry (CR 122.6, 614.1c), not after it; counters are not copiable (CR 707.2), so the source's own are never copied. The amount is read once for the resolution (CR 608.2h: Ochre Jelly's TriggerRemembered$CardCounters.P1P1/HalfDown reads the dead Jelly's last known counters, the delayed program's LKI); B <= 0 is a plain copy, and a token doubler's extra copies each get the counters. No copy exceptions, CopyFlags or NumCopies$ (kgen refuses them beside the rider); a copy with an as-enters choice (a colour, a type) parks on it and enters with the counters when answered (raGenTokChoice); an Aura, a clone election, or a choice beside a non-constant amount stalls rather than dropping the counters. Ochre Jelly, A-Ochre Jelly, Littjara Mirrorlake."},
	{"ext:Recruit", "OpExt ExtRecruit", "The Hobbit's Recruit action (gorge effRecruit, DB$ Recruit): the resolving controller draws a card, then discards a card (one pick in hand order, ChRecruitDiscard, CanonKind discard; no ask when the hand holds one card, nothing when empty), then creates one 1/1 white Human Soldier token only if a nonland card was discarded. Touches no remembered set. Esgaroth Garrison, Great Gilded Boat, Lake-town Lookout, Long Lake Nuisance, Patient Instructor, Sound the Trumpets, The Mountain-king's Return, The Queen of Dale."},
	{"ext:Cumulative", "OpExt ExtCumulative (C the instructions to skip when the source is gone)", "The head of a cumulative upkeep trigger's body (CR 702.24a; Mystic Remora): the source, if it is still the permanent that triggered on the battlefield, gets an age counter through the ordinary counter placement (an AddCounter replacement applies, as gorge's CounterChange emit); if it is gone the next C instructions (the payment and the sacrifice) are skipped. The UnlessPaid after it charges its generic cost once per age counter now on the source, as the trigger's own pay-or-decline ask (gorge cumulative_pay / cumulative_sac, canonically trigger_cost_pay / trigger_cost_decline), and the Sacrifice of the source behind it runs on a decline. A generic cost lowers as Mana with the amount times the age counters; a coloured or hybrid mana cost carries the cost of one counter and B = 2 (kop.CumulativeScaled), which the kernel multiplies by the age counters when it poses the ask (gorge scaleCost; a hybrid pip is announced once per counter, up to four, dirac/trig_cumulativepay.go); a life, default discard or land or creature sacrifice cost is the matching UnlessPaid with the amount times the age counters; any other cumulative upkeep cost refuses. With B = 1 it heads an echo trigger instead (CR 702.30a; Cradle Guard, Mogg War Marshal, Avalanche Riders): the same gone-source skip, no age counter, and the UnlessPaid behind it charges the printed mana cost (generic and coloured pips) once (gorge echo_pay / echo_sac, canonically trigger_cost_pay / trigger_cost_decline). dirac/trig_cumulative.go, trig_echo.go."},
	{"ext:NumTimes", "OpExt ExtNumTimes (A unit generic, B packed unit pips, C max, Skip the decline jump)", "A printed trigger's own \"pay {unit} up to N times\" announcement (gorge triggeredCostNumTimesAsk): the controller announces 0..m, m the most repetitions (up to AnnounceMax$ N) whose total the potential mana covers, kept as the resolution's X; 0 declines and skips the rest of the body. The IfPaid that follows charges the unit X times. With no repetition payable nothing is asked and the IfPaid poses its decline-only ask. Tranquil Frillback."},
	{"ext:ChooseName", "OpExt ExtChooseName", "An as-enters nonland card-name choice, the first instruction of an enters program (CR 614.12, 201.4; gorge's ETB NameCard, Defined$ You, ValidCards$ Card.nonLand): the entering permanent's controller chooses the name of one real nonland card of the matchup (a ChGenName decision, mode = the card's CardID, Table.NameCards ascending, gorge's sorted name list over the same cards), asked as the colour choice is, and the answer is kept in the permanent's chosen byte as that CardID (a permanent that left holds nothing, CR 400.7). A matchup holding a multi-face card beside a name chooser is refused when it is built, and the pool table plays the chooser inert when it holds a multi-face card or a nonland card with a CardID of 255 or more. An activation is matched on the source's printed name, so a copy of a named card or a face-down source would differ from gorge, which reads the current name. Read by a Tf4NamedCast SpellCast line. Kai Winn, Faithless Leader. B = 3 offers only the nonland names among the hands of the seats still in the game but the chooser (Alhammarret, High Arbiter: ETB RevealHand Player.Opponent | RememberRevealed, NameCard ChooseFromDefinedCards$ Remembered, Cleanup; the reveal is public and poses no decision), and poses no ask at all when no nonland card was shown, as gorge poses none for an empty set; the CantBeCast B&CantCastNamed read compares the cast card with the answer."},
	{"ext:EachDamage", "OpExt ExtEachDamage (F, B, C)", "Every battlefield permanent matching F (seat 0 first, entry order; read once) -- or, with damager target slots in C's high byte (a bit per slot), the objects of those slots legal as the resolution started, in pick order, still on the battlefield and matching F when set -- deals B damage to the object in Ref C's low byte (a target, or Self), B = 0 meaning each damager's own power (Count$CardPower), in one damage batch whose hits name their own sources: replacement, prevention, deathtouch and lifelink per source, lifelink gained once per source, damage triggers after (gorge effEachDamage, DefinedDamagers$ Valid <filter>, ParentTarget or a one-slot Targeted). A Targeted union over two or more slots, EachToItself$, ToEachOther$, ValidCards$ and player recipients refuse. Case of the Gateway Express, Moonlight Hunt; Common Goal, Band Together."},
	{"ext:DmgMark", "OpExt ExtDmgMark (Obj the damaged player)", "An Effect's `Event$ DamageDone | ValidSource$ Card,Emblem | ValidTarget$ Player.IsRemembered,Permanent.ControlledBy Player.IsRemembered` replacement whose body doubles the damage (`ReplaceCount$DamageAmount/Twice`), Duration$ UntilYourNextTurn, RememberObjects$ TriggeredTarget (gorge replacement_damage.go reads the captured players): the resolving controller marks the player in Obj, one genState.dmk bit per (controller, player), and every damage event to that player or a permanent they control is doubled once per live mark; the controller's marks end at the cleanup before their next turn. The same controller marking the same player again while it is live stalls (StallDmgMark); an event the mark and another damage replacement both match stalls (StallDmgMarkOrder: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order, which the mark has no object candidate for). Lightning, Army of One. With C = kop.DmgMarkBySource (no Obj) the mark is the resolving controller's sources instead of a recipient: until end of turn every damage event dealt by a source they control, to anything, is doubled once per live mark (an Effect with no Duration$, ValidSource$ Card.YouCtrl,Emblem.YouCtrl, ValidTarget$ Permanent,Player): one genState.dmk bit per controller, cleared at the cleanup; a second one while it is live stalls (StallDmgMark). Quest for Pure Flame."},
	{"ext:PreventNext", "OpExt ExtPreventNext", "Prevent the next B damage that would be dealt this turn to the one player or permanent Obj (gorge effPreventDamage's DamageDone shield, CR 615.7): the shield prevents min(left, amount) of each event, is spent by it and is dropped when spent; the damage left through feeds lifelink, infect and the damage triggers. A recipient off the battlefield or out of the game takes none; an amount of zero or less installs nothing. Three prevention records a turn beside the colour and scope ones (genState.prevCol; a fourth stalls StallPrevCol); an amount of 255 or more, or an event another damage replacement is also a candidate for (a second shield on the recipient, a colour or scope prevention, a SHIELD counter, a printed prevention, a doubler, a plus-N, a prevent-and-mill or self-damage replacement on the battlefield, a damage mark) stalls StallPrevNext: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order and it changes what is prevented. Two or more shields on one recipient are asked in order (damageTo and combat passes; other damage sites stall). Combat events are dealt in gorge's assignment order while a shield is live. C 1: combat damage only (Decorated Griffin). C 2: all damage, no amount: an unbounded shield (col 255) that prevents every event to the recipient and is never spent, ended by the recipient leaving the battlefield or the turn change (Shielded Passage, Indestructible Aura, Godtoucher, Djeru's Resolve: gorge's ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield Effect); beside a second shield it stalls StallPrevNext. C 4 and 8 (Awe Strike, ValidSource$ Card.IsRemembered with a PreventionEffect$ True rider whose body gains the prevented life and exiles the Effect): C 4 keys the shield on the damage source, the remembered target creature (it requires C 2; the record is spent by the first event from the creature and the creature leaving the battlefield ends it first), and C 8 runs the gain rider beside any live rider record. The upper C bits name the several-recipient and rider forms: 256 installs a shield on every battlefield permanent matching F; 512 on every living player; 1024 on the target in Obj and each other creature sharing a colour with it (Radiance); 2048 on each still-legal target of the divided slot in W with the share announced for it (DividedAsYouChoose$; a division the kernel must ask at resolution stalls StallPrevNext); 4096/8192/16384 run the rider at each application: +1/+1 counters on the rider's target, the amount accumulated for the next end step's P0P1 counters (only while the target is still a creature when the body has IsPresent$ Creature.IsRemembered, Scars of the Veteran), and the prevented amount dealt as the shield's source to the rider's target (PreventionSubAbility$ with ShieldEffectTarget$ Targeted, ParentTarget or You; W is the parent target). A capacity past three records stalls StallPrevCol, and each rider's own order ask stalls StallPrevRider. A random recipient stays refused. Healing Salve, Alabaster Potion, Battlefield Medic, Combat Medic, Awe Strike, Test of Faith, Temper, Sacred Boon, Scars of the Veteran, Acolyte's Reward, Vengeful Archon, Angel of Salvation, Embolden, Pollen Remedy, Remedy, Serra's Hymn, Kitsune Palliator, Samite Censer-Bearer, Wojek Apothecary, Fylgja."},
	{"ext:DmgRedirect", "OpExt ExtDmgRedirect (Obj the recipient, C kop.DmgRedirect*)", "An Effect's DamageDone redirect replacement. DmgRedirectNext (Nomads en-Kor, Warrior en-Kor: `ValidTarget$ Creature.EffectSource`, body `DB$ ReplaceSplitDamage | DamageTarget$ Remembered`, Duration$ UntilHostLeavesPlayOrEOT): the next 1 damage to the resolving source this turn is dealt to the target in Obj instead, as a new damage event from the same source (it meets protection, prevention and doubling again; the held event keeps the rest). DmgRedirectScope (Gideon's Sacrifice: `ValidTarget$ You,Permanent.YouCtrl`, body `DB$ ReplaceEffect | VarName$ Affected | VarValue$ Remembered`): all damage this turn to the resolving controller and their permanents is dealt to the chosen permanent in Obj instead. The record ends with the turn, its pool, and its host or recipient leaving (genState.redir, four a turn; a fifth stalls StallRedirCap); an event a record and another damage replacement both match stalls (StallRedirOrder: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order, which the records are no candidate of), as does a redirect of an infect or wither source or inside a combat order walk. Combat events are redirected per assignment. Nomads en-Kor, Warrior en-Kor, Gideon's Sacrifice."},
	{"ext:PreventDamageScope", "OpExt ExtPreventDamageScope", "All damage that would be dealt this turn to the resolving controller and/or the creatures they control (C bits kop.PrevScope*), optionally only by creature sources on the battlefield (PrevScopeSrcCreature) or by sources of given colours (the C bits above PrevScopeColourShift), to any recipient (PrevScopeAll: no ValidTarget$) and combat only (PrevScopeCombat) or combat and noncombat (gorge effEffect's bodyless DamageDone Prevent$ replacement in the Command zone): one more genState.prevCol record per resolution, each its own CR 616.1 order candidate (three a turn; a fourth stalls StallPrevCol). With PrevScopeFiltered the damage source's filter is F and the recipient permanents' is B.N (the record keeps the bit; the kernel finds the instruction from the Effect's source card, repl_prevscopefilter.go); PrevScopeOppPlayer / PrevScopeAnyPlayer name the opponents / every player as recipients. A high op (kop/ops.go). With PrevScopeGain (an instruction-only bit; the record keeps a rider byte, genState.prevX, repl_prevx.go) the record's controller gains life equal to the damage each event prevents (a lone matching record; beside any other candidate, a PreventNext shield, a can't-prevent static or a parked ask it stalls StallPrevRider); Chant of Vitu-Ghazi. Fog family (Heavy Fog, Pack Leader), Eerie Interference, The Needs of the Many, Summon: Alexander, Ethereal Haze, Surge of Salvation, Loyal Unicorn."},
	{"ext:TurnRepl", "OpExt ExtTurnRepl (C kop.TurnReplExileOpp, TurnReplPlusCreatureCtr, TurnReplUncounter, TurnReplUncounterCreature, TurnReplPlayerHex or TurnReplHexUB)", "An Effect's until-end-of-turn replacement over a player's side of the board. C=TurnReplExileOpp: `DB$ Effect | ReplacementEffects$` with one `Event$ Moved | ValidLKI$ Creature.OppCtrl | Origin$ Battlefield | Destination$ Graveyard` body `DB$ ChangeZone | Defined$ ReplacedCard | Origin$ Battlefield | Destination$ Exile` -- every creature an opponent of the controller controls that would die this turn is exiled instead, one that enters after the Effect resolved included (a scope record in the kernel's exile-instead table, read by dieZone beside the per-object marks; competing with another exile-instead effect it stalls StallReplLeave). C=TurnReplPlusCreatureCtr: one `Event$ AddCounter | ValidCard$ Creature.YouCtrl+inZoneBattlefield | ValidCounterType$ P1P1` body `DB$ ReplaceCounter | ValidCounterType$ P1P1 | ChooseCounter$ True | Amount$ Y` with `Y: ReplaceCount$CounterNum/Plus.1` -- one more +1/+1 counter on a creature the controller controls, a per-player count apart from ExtCounterPlusEOT's (it is one more plus candidate in the CR 616.1 order ask beside Boimler's and a doubler's). C=TurnReplUncounter / TurnReplUncounterCreature: one bodyless `Event$ Counter | ValidSA$ Spell.YouCtrl` (or `Spell.Creature+wasCastByYou`) `Layer$ CantHappen` line -- every spell (creature spell) the controller controls this turn, cast before or after the Effect, can't be countered (a scope record read by OpCounter and ward through uncounterable; two live records matching one spell stall StallUncounterOrder). Veil of Summer, Domri, Anarch of Bolas. C=TurnReplPlayerHex: the player half of a Pump `Defined$ You & Valid <permanents> | KW$ Hexproof` -- the controller can't be targeted by an opponent this turn (Dawn's Truce, Lazotep Plating, Surge of Salvation). C=TurnReplHexUB: Veil of Summer's `KW$ Hexproof:Black & Hexproof:Blue` over `You & Valid Permanent.YouCtrl` -- the controller and each permanent they control as it resolves have hexproof from blue and from black (CR 702.11d; the permanents in the mechHexUB slot plane, a later loss of abilities takes the grant). All end at cleanup. Malicious Eclipse, Prairie Dog."},
	{"ext:CounterPlusEOT", "OpExt ExtCounterPlusEOT", "Until end of turn, if one or more counters would be put on a permanent the resolving controller controls, that many plus one of each of those kinds are put on it instead (Brad Boimler, Eager Ensign's tap-triggered `DB$ Effect | ReplacementEffects$` with one `Event$ AddCounter | ActiveZones$ Battlefield | ValidCard$ Permanent.YouCtrl+inZoneBattlefield` body whose `DB$ ReplaceCounter | ChooseCounter$ True | Amount$ X` has `X: ReplaceCount$CounterNum/Plus.1`; gorge effEffect's AddCounter replacement with no ValidCounterType$, so every kind matches, rules/replacement_match.go). A per-player count in genState.plusCtr, one per activation, set by the resolution and cleared at cleanup; it applies through the ordinary counter-replacement path, so it is its own CR 616.1 order candidate against a doubler (both stall StallReplCtr) and the effect's ActiveZones$ gate is not consulted after it resolves, even if the source leaves. Only the exact shape lowers; every other Effect+AddCounter shape keeps its named refusal. Brad Boimler, Eager Ensign."},
	{"ext:PreventColor", "OpExt ExtPreventColor", "The resolving controller chooses a colour (ChGenColor, all five); all damage sources of that colour would deal this turn is prevented, combat and noncombat (gorge effChooseColor, then effEffect's bodyless DamageDone Prevent$ replacement over ValidSource$ Card.ChosenColor): a genState.prevCol record per resolution (three a turn; a fourth stalls StallPrevCol), each its own CR 616.1 order candidate, the same card resolving again moving its records to the new colour (gorge reads the card's live ChosenColor). A high op (kop/ops.go). Prismatic Strands."},
}
